analyzeStrand -- analyze the (a+1)-st constant strand of F over ZZ
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        L = analyzeStrand(F,a)
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, the nonminimal resolution of a
        carpet over large prime
      * a, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, a+1 is the degree of the strand
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the diagonal entries of the Smith
        normal form of a the crucial matrix

Description
===========

Starting from a nonminimal resolution F of the carpet over a larger finite
prime field, we lift the complex to the integers, and compute the diagonal
entries of the Smith normal form. The critical constrand strand for a carpet of
type (a,b) with a>=b is the a+1-st strand. Green's conjecture for carpet says
that the map has maximal rank over QQ.

