computeBound -- compute the bound for the good types in case of k resonance
***************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (a,b) = computeBound(a1,b1,k)
        c = computeBound k
  * Inputs:
      * a1, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * b1, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, type of the degenerate K3
      * k, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the resonance
  * Outputs:
      * a, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * b, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, minimal good type
      * c, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, lower bound for good a,b

Description
===========

The iterated mapping over the relative resolution of X_e(a,b) in the resonance
scroll has betti numbers in a range of a general 2k-gonal canonical curve of
genus a+b+1, if a,b are large enough, see ES2018. We compute the minimal type
$(a,b) \equiv (a1,b1) \mod  k$ where this becomes true.

In the second version c is the minimal value of a,b's for all congruence
classes mod k. We conjecture that c=k^2-k.

