Scrolls -- Option for carpet, canonicalCarpet
*********************************************

Description
===========

The default is Scrolls => false. If the option Scrolls=>true is given, then a
triple is returned, with the ideal first followed by xmat and ymat, the smaller
and larger of the scrolls containing the carpet.

Functions with optional argument named Scrolls:
===============================================

  * "canonicalCarpet(...,Scrolls=>...)" -- see *note canonicalCarpet:
    canonicalCarpet, -- Carpet of given genus and Clifford index
  * "carpet(...,Scrolls=>...)" -- see *note carpet: carpet, -- Ideal of the
    unique Gorenstein double structure on a 2-dimensional scroll

For the programmer
==================

The object *note Scrolls: Scrolls, is a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,.

